GtkBuilder can only resolve a template type that was never registered by
looking up <type>_get_type() in the executable. On Linux this works by
accident: the network panel depends on gmodule-2.0, whose pkg-config flags
add -Wl,--export-dynamic to the whole binary. The network panel isn't built
here, so CcEntryFeedback is unknown and building the template fails (crash
when clicking Password / Add User). Register the type explicitly, as
cc-enterprise-login-dialog.c already does.

Index: panels/system/users/cc-password-dialog.c
--- panels/system/users/cc-password-dialog.c.orig
+++ panels/system/users/cc-password-dialog.c
@@ -450,6 +450,8 @@ cc_password_dialog_class_init (CcPasswor
 
         object_class->dispose = cc_password_dialog_dispose;
 
+        g_type_ensure (CC_TYPE_ENTRY_FEEDBACK);
+
         gtk_widget_class_set_template_from_resource (widget_class, "/org/gnome/control-center/system/users/cc-password-dialog.ui");
 
         gtk_widget_class_bind_template_child (widget_class, CcPasswordDialog, action_login_radio);
